# The viewer's bundles embed these as STRINGS (esbuild's `loader: { ".css": "text" }`),
# so their line endings end up inside the artifact. Without a rule here a Windows
# checkout gets CRLF, the bundle carries CRLF, and the same sources produce a
# different artifact on Linux. eol=lf forces LF in the WORKING TREE, not merely in
# the index, which is what the build reads.
*.css text eol=lf
